<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Scandinavia and the Baltic</p><h1 class="st-title">Republic of Uhtua</h1><p class="st-meta">1919 CE – 1920 CE · capital Uhtua</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Finnish-backed provisional government of East Karelia in 1919-1920, based in the village of Uhtua, which sought union with Finland.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-revolution">Russian Revolution</a>, Finnish nationalists hoped to join <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-karelia">East Karelia</a>, homeland of much <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kalevala">Kalevala</a> folk poetry, to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-finland">Finland</a>. Finnish volunteer expeditions entered the region in 1918-1919, and in 1919 local <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/karelians">Karelians</a> and Finnish activists set up a Provisional Government of East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karelia">Karelia</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uhtua">Uhtua</a> (now Kalevala).</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The government controlled only the area around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/uhtua">Uhtua</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/white-sea">White Sea</a> <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/karelians">Karelia</a> region. It held a meeting of Karelian representatives that voted for separation from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, issued its own stamps and relied on Finnish volunteers and supplies.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> retook the area in 1920, and the government fled to <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/republic-of-finland">Finland</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-tartu-finnish-russian">Treaty of Tartu</a> of 1920 left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-karelia">East Karelia</a> in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Soviet Russia</a>, which had already set up a Karelian Labour Commune that June. A further uprising in 1921-1922 also failed, and the area later formed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/karelo-finnish-soviet-socialist-republic">Karelo-Finnish Soviet Socialist Republic</a>.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/republic-of-uhtua.jpg" alt="Republic of Uhtua" width="320" height="179"><figcaption>Image: Fenn-O-maniC · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:State_flag_of_East_Karelia_(1920-1922).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1919 CE – 1920 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Uhtua</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Karelian, Finnish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/russia">Russia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>East Karelia Republic, Uhtuan tasavalta</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1920&amp;focus=republic-of-uhtua" aria-label="Republic of Uhtua on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5298 45 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Republic of Uhtua lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5618 301L5521 419M5618 301L5820 533"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5521 419h0M5820 533h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5618 301h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5618 301h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1920&amp;focus=republic-of-uhtua">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

